--TEST--
a balanced directional scope in a string literal compiles and survives byte for byte — ADR 0087 § 1
--FILE--
<?nvs
// ADR 0087 § 1: only an *unterminated* scope is rejected. Legitimate
// mixed-direction text isolates its Latin run and closes the isolate, which is
// what makes rejecting the rest affordable — this case is the one that fails if
// the rule is ever widened to a blanket ban on the eleven code points.
string $message = "خطأ: ⁦user_id⁩ غير موجود";
echo $message, "\n";
// A comment may hold one too, and a stray terminator closes nothing.
string $marks = "‏right ‎left‬";
echo $marks, "\n";
--EXPECT--
خطأ: ⁦user_id⁩ غير موجود
‏right ‎left‬
